&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.reachdesk.com/candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;www.reachdesk.com/candidate-privacy-policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Moniepoint Inc. is Africa’s all-in-one financial platform, helping 20 million businesses and individuals access seamless payments, banking, credit, cross-border, and business management tools each month.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Nigeria’s largest merchant acquirer, we power most of the country’s point-of-sale (POS) transactions. Through our subsidiaries, Moniepoint Inc. processes over $250 billion in digital payment transaction value annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Moniepoint, data is at the core of everything we do. We are a customer-centric company, and your work will enable our teams to make informed, data-driven decisions that directly impact the success of our business. We are seeking a data-driven, impact-oriented Senior Data Scientist to power Moniepoint’s consumer lending decisions at scale. You will build the models, experiments, and insights that shape how we acquire, underwrite, and retain millions of customers across Nigeria and Africa.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is pivotal in driving our pricing, credit limit modelling, and credit model deployment strategy in a growing business with unparalleled opportunities to give access to millions of customers.&amp;nbsp;You’ll collaborate with our amazing Consumer Credit team and drive how we think about risk ranking, product offering, and data infrastructure to create the best personalised offers for our customers. You’ll be responsible for building our first suite of credit risk models and help drive a culture of how we should think about machine learning vs more traditional methods - bringing fresh thinking to inspire both the team and our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sitting at the intersection of data science, credit risk, and product, you’ll translate complex data into actionable decisions that drive growth with healthy portfolio performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Curious about what makes Moniepoint an incredible place to work? &lt;a href=&quot;https://moniepoint.com/blog&quot;&gt;Check out posts on how we cultivate a culture of innovation, teamwork, and growth.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deploy credit scoring, affordability, and behavioural models to support underwriting, pricing, and collections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run experiments to optimise approval rates, loss rates, and profitability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product squads to embed decision logic into real-time systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure data quality, compliance, and ethical use of models across all decisioning processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor product squads on best practices in experimentation and data-driven decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide models to optimise outcomes in collections, churn management and user retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We would love to hear from you if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable with Statistics and have a Degree or qualifications&amp;nbsp; in a quantitative field (Statistics, Mathematics, Engineering or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have +5 years of experience in data science, decision science, or risk analytics within financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of credit risk, consumer lending, and regulatory considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in SQL and at least one modelling/programming language (Python, R)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with A/B testing, machine learning, collections modelling and churn management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex analyses into clear recommendations for business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership mindset and comfort working in fast-paced, cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we can offer you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture: We put our people first and prioritise the well-being of every team member. We’ve built a company where all opinions carry weight and where all voices are heard. We value and respect each other and always look out for one another. Above all, we are human.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning: We have a learning and development-focused environment with an emphasis on knowledge sharing, training, and regular internal technical talks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation: You’ll receive an attractive salary, pension, health insurance, monthly bonuses, plus other benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to expect in the hiring process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A preliminary phone call with the recruiter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A coding exercise on HackerRank - covering core data science theory (math, statistics, linear algebra) and Python fundamentals (data structures &amp;amp; algorithms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A take-home assignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A technical interview with a Lead in our Data Science Team to review your take-home assignment in depth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A behavioural and technical interview with the hiring manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Moniepoint is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and candidates.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Moniepoint Inc. is Africa’s all-in-one financial platform, helping 20 million businesses and individuals access seamless payments, banking, credit, cross-border, and business management tools each month.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Nigeria’s largest merchant acquirer, we power most of the country’s point-of-sale (POS) transactions. Through our subsidiaries, Moniepoint Inc. processes over $250 billion in digital payment transaction value annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why United Kingdom&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UK is home to our headquarters where more than 70 team members are based. Our London office is located at Sea Containers, just by London Bridge - this is also where a significant number of our most senior leaders sit, which makes it a natural base for a Head of Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So, now we are looking for our Head of Engineering, Rewards to join us in United Kingdom.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rewards is one of the most strategically important platforms at Moniepoint, and it is being built into a dedicated charter with its own engineering and product leadership. The platform sits at the centre of our retention strategy across a user base of approximately 23 million people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today the platform does one thing: cashback. It works, but it has barely scratched the surface of what rewards can be, and the cashback product itself is not yet built to the depth it deserves. The ambition is to evolve it into a full rewards, retention, engagement and personalisation platform — and to do that across the full 360 degrees of our network. That means rewards for our business customers, rewards for our consumer customers, and rewards for the sales agents who drive our distribution. Very few companies get to design this from close to a blank page at this scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Head of Engineering owns that platform end to end. You will inherit a team of nine engineers, including an Engineering Manager, and build the organisation out from there — the current expectation is a minimum of three product units and upwards of 25 people, though the eventual shape is genuinely yours to define. Your first objective is to get the best possible performance out of the cashback product we already have. From there, you will work with Growth, Sales and Marketing to determine what we build for acquisition and retention, and roll it out across every customer we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a consumer-facing product engineering role, and that is the most important thing to understand about it. Rewards is won or lost on experimentation, personalisation, and the quality of the experience in a customer&#39;s hands. We are looking for a leader who has built and shipped direct-to-consumer products at scale, who is fluent in experimentation and A/B testing, and who has real depth in front-end and mobile engineering — not a purely backend platform leader.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Moniepoint runs a Domain CTO model. We view our Heads of Engineering as the CTO of their domain: you own the technical roadmap, the architecture, the delivery, and the organisation beneath you. You will have full autonomy over engineering strategy, architecture, hiring, operating cadence and roadmap trade-offs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report functionally to our Group CTO, with a dual reporting line into the Product leader for Rewards. That second line is a delivery relationship rather than a seniority one — engineering and product are peers here, and you will build the team to full capacity together. Your responsibilities as Head of Engineering, Rewards includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the technical strategy, architecture and roadmap for the Rewards Platform end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the performance, reliability and depth of the existing cashback product as an immediate first priority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolving cashback into a broader rewards, retention, engagement and personalisation platform serving business customers, consumer customers and sales agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building the engineering organisation from its current base - structuring product units, hiring engineers and Engineering Managers, and leading through those managers as the team scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establishing a strong experimentation culture: A/B testing, cohort analysis, and measurement that lets the team learn quickly what actually changes customer behaviour.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with Growth, Sales and Marketing to translate acquisition and retention objectives into product and engineering initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the customer-facing experience of rewards across mobile and web, including how quickly and reliably customers receive what they have earned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define architecture standards, engineering processes and quality metrics, and own the engineering health of the domain — incidents, production defects, deployment frequency, change failure rate, and developer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the platform to serve customers across multiple geographies as Moniepoint expands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product to define the rewards-specific metrics and OKRs that do not yet exist, and hold the team to them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct-to-consumer product engineering at scale. You have built and shipped products used directly by large consumer audiences, and you understand what moves engagement and retention. This is the defining requirement of the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine front-end and mobile depth. You have led or personally built consumer-facing mobile and web experiences. A backend-only background, however strong, is not what this role needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experimentation and growth engineering. Hands-on experience running A/B tests, feature flagging, and measurement frameworks, and using the results to drive product decisions rather than to justify them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience managing managers — leading an engineering organisation through other engineering leaders, not a single team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on technical leadership. You are still close to the code. We expect a meaningful proportion of hands-on engineering time and technical credibility with the engineers you lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of overall software engineering experience, with at least 5 years leading engineering teams through growth phases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with our backend environment — Java and Spring Boot — and the ability to lead backend engineers credibly, even if it is not where your own depth sits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and scaling an engineering organisation from a small base, including hiring and developing Engineering Managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration with commercial stakeholders — growth, marketing and sales — and the ability to translate business objectives into engineering work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rewards, loyalty, gamification, personalisation or growth platform experience is a strong advantage but is not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fintech or payments experience is an advantage, not a requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cultural Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As well, we assess every candidate across eight dimensions that define how great leaders operate at Moniepoint. We look for evidence of all eight throughout the process, not just in a single conversation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Obsession: Build deep empathy for users. Solve problems intuitively, and fix root causes, not just tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft: Master the fundamentals. Reason from first principles, make trade-offs explicit, and raise the bar on quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systemisation: Turn repeating decisions into scalable mechanisms. Reduce cognitive load and raise engineering quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Urgency: Move with disciplined speed. Act autonomously within scope, remove friction, and escalate risks early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership: Treat the platform as your own. Take initiative across boundaries and follow through without reminders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No Ego: Put the mission first. Share credit, welcome debate, and never protect status over team outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candour: Surface uncomfortable truths and risks early. Intelligent failure is welcome; concealment is not.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrity: Stay truthful and ethically consistent. Refuse toxic behavior. Performance without integrity is unacceptable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like In The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The existing cashback product performing measurably better — faster, more reliable, and more compelling to customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A credible rewards platform roadmap defined with Product, and the first initiatives beyond cashback shipped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A functioning experimentation practice, where the team ships, measures and learns on a short cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An engineering organisation built out from its current base, with a strong bench of Engineering Managers and senior engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rewards established as a measurable contributor to retention and engagement across the customer base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear architecture standards and engineering processes in place across the product units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A rare blank page. The platform exists, but almost everything it could become is still ahead of it, and you will define what that is.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct influence on retention across a base of roughly 23 million users, at one of the largest and fastest-growing digital banks in Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full autonomy as the CTO of your domain, with the backing to build the organisation you think the problem needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be part of a mission-driven company expanding access to financial services for millions of businesses and individuals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What To Expect In The Hiring Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;60 minute High level System Design round with one of our Engineering Managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;60 minute Panel Interview with 2 of our Head of Engineering leaders. 30 minutes focused on a technical deep dive into your CV and into a project or system you built in the past. 30 minutes focused on testing for leadership attributes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;60 minute Stakeholder Management Round with one of our Product Heads/VPs, focused on your stakeholder management and collaboration skills with product and business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;60 minute Technical round and Culture fit interview with our Co-founder &amp;amp; Group CTO (the hiring manager).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Moniepoint is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and candidates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hi! We’re hipages, an ASX-listed tech company and Australia’s #1 digital platform connecting households with trusted home improvement businesses. We&#39;re on a mission to transform the home improvement industry to build better lives for everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With teams across Australia, New Zealand, the Philippines and Vietnam, we work as one team with a shared purpose. We’re proud to be a certified &lt;strong&gt;Great Place to Work&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;WORK180’s #1 Employer for Women&lt;/strong&gt;. At hipages, you’ll find real impact, career growth and a workplace where everyone belongs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll play a crucial role in supporting the hipages marketplace by developing our analytics engineering capabilities. Working alongside a talented data team to create immense value for the business and contribute to the development and execution of hipages&#39; commercial strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your experience and expertise will help us discover new ways of operating in the world of data modelling and business intelligence. You&#39;ll design and support the deployment of end-to-end data models, data products as well as develop and maintain internal analytics capabilities within our data platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is vital in scaling our current data architecture and capabilities on DBT, Databricks and Tableau to enable self-service analytics. This role will be reporting into the Head of Commercial and Data Analytics giving that mentorship and executive buy-in to ensure this role is a success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior, hands-on role leading a craft pod of three analytics engineers, yet setting direction across a much wider community, acting as the technical authority on what &quot;good&quot; data design looks like.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join our Data team?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💻 Hybrid working model &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🪴 In-house Talent Development team to prioritise personal and career growth &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💰 Competitive salary, benefits and perks, plus equity via our Employee Share Program &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🤸 Cross-functional collaboration across Product, Engineering, Marketing and Commercial teams &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will add value:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; People Management&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and line-manage a team of 2 Analytics Engineers, fostering a culture of technical excellence, continuous learning, and open collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape analytics engineering practices across hipages, establishing standards for reproducibility, observability, style guides, and contributions to our data handbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educate data teams and broader business stakeholders on analytics engineering best practices and self-serve capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Architectural &amp;amp; Technical Execution&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary advocate for dbt while providing technical leadership throughout the Databricks and Tableau BI landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, design, and implement scalable, high-performance data models in dbt and Databricks in close collaboration with Data Analysts and Data Engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, establish, and enforce&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;data&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;contracts&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;between software engineering producers and downstream data models to eliminate breaking upstream schema changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Delivery &amp;amp; Engineering Excellence&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply modern software engineering best practices (CI/CD, Git version control, automated testing) to iteratively deliver reliable data products and platform capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive end-to-end data quality, governance, SLAs, and consistency across our analytics and data science ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify operational bottlenecks, optimize query execution, and streamline data pipelines to enhance overall system performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee comprehensive documentation of data architecture, pipeline lineage, and analytical workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Technical &amp;amp; Architectural&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Statistics, Mathematics, Physics, Economics or a related quantitative qualification or relevant equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced SQL with deep experience designing and building scalable data architectures (Kimball dimensional modeling, Data Vault, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on mastery of dbt (Data Build Tool) and strong experience with enterprise cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience defining, enforcing, or implementing Data Contracts to manage producer-consumer interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience developing and governing semantic layers in AI and BI tools like Tableau&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Strategic Execution&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven capability to manage direct reports, work independently, and drive cross-functional alignment with excellent communication and conflict-resolution skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable navigating ambiguity, managing priorities, and delivering iterative value in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about data culture, with a proven ability to translate complex data structures into clear, actionable narratives for technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to two-sided marketplace dynamics, network metrics, or high-velocity event-driven data ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Data Science teams to build feature stores, orchestrate pipelines (e.g., Airflow, Databricks Workflows), or support ML model deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest or experience in shaping data for AI/LLM consumption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at hipages:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re more than just a workplace. We’re a place where you can be yourself, do great work and grow your career. Recognised as a Great Place to Work, our inclusive, supportive culture helps people thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll use the best tools and tech, with real impact on our products and customers. We invest in your development and lead with coaching, not micromanagement – it’s why 85% of our team say their leader is great.&amp;nbsp;And there’s more:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diverse, collaborative teams that love solving problems &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agile squads, hackathons, off-sites and roadshows &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extra leave for birthdays, volunteering, and more &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthy snacks, continental breakfast and fresh fruit &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sydney CBD office near Town Hall and Gadigal Stations &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailored growth support, mentoring and stretch projects &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A vibrant social scene - we work hard and have fun doing it &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prioritise Diversity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At hipages, innovation and collaboration thrive in diverse and inclusive teams. We don’t expect you to know everything - we care more about who you are as a person, a team member, and a leader.&amp;nbsp;We’re proud to be endorsed by WORK180 for supporting women’s careers and we value diversity across culture, age, gender identity and sexual orientation.&amp;nbsp;Research shows that men often apply when they meet just 60% of the criteria, while women and minority groups wait until they tick every box. If you think you’d be a great fit - even if you don’t meet every requirement - we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re also a Circle Back Initiative Employer, which means we commit to responding to every applicant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/ntj8ttXP88s&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
