&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on your performance, we can discuss further opportunities at Picnic!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Where you can make an impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt; – Optimize the backbone of our operations, from fulfillment centers to last-mile delivery and demand forecasting across Europe. Think: automating international delivery forecasts for growth markets like France.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech&lt;/strong&gt; – Build scalable backend systems, cutting-edge AI workflows, and internal tooling that power our entire platform. Think: building AI agent workflows (using Python, Claude, and SQL).&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consumer&lt;/strong&gt; – Drive customer growth and strategic category development across our markets. Think: optimizing search algorithms for recipe discovery and running deep-dive analyses on customer retention and membership strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Why Picnic&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow as we grow.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;From day one, you’ll take ownership of real business projects that affect millions of customers, gaining hands-on experience.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn from top minds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Work alongside driven, talented mentors in a high-energy environment. You&#39;ll build, solve problems, and celebrate together, from our legendary Friday drinks to team events and parties.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kickstart your career.&lt;/strong&gt; Earn a competitive student salary with flexible working hours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Picnic Perks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀&lt;strong&gt;Every expert was once a beginner!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’ll have plenty of chances to grow, whether it’s through our casual Lunch &amp;amp; Learn sessions or team specific trainings. We’re especially keen on keeping great talent around: perform well as a working student, and we would love to explore&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;transitioning you into a full-time role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌍&lt;strong&gt;Make a difference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You’ll work in an awesome startup environment with the freedom to drive your own projects and create a visible impact. Our fully electric vehicles and sustainable business model mean you’ll also be contributing to making the world a better place!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🤝&lt;strong&gt;Teamwork makes the dream work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;With more than 80 nationalities across 3 countries, you’ll be part of a diverse company with plenty of cool stuff to get involved with, from board game evenings to after-work drinks to our company ski trip and more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🥗Fresh Lunch, coffee, and snacks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our offices are equipped with fully-fledged coffee bars and a kitchen and chefs. They prepare delicious fresh and warm lunches every day so you can keep your energy up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💪&lt;strong&gt;Stay healthy &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Mental health is important. As well as having the option to speak with Picnic colleagues who act as confidential advisors, our collaboration with OpenUp gives you easy access to professional psychologists, along with workshops and materials. &lt;br&gt;There are plenty of sports communities and events to get involved with, from tennis to yoga to climbing!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰&lt;strong&gt;Attractive package&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We offer competitive compensation and a pension plan that looks out for your future self.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-intro-section&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section-inner&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;entry-intro&quot;&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-intro-section&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In a nutshell&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;As our UX researcher, you will work collaboratively with Data Analysts, Product Owners, and Designers to develop the full user experience of Picnic’s products. With an open personality, you’re able to empathize with end-users on a weekly basis, whether that’s by guiding users through prototypes or investigating a new topic.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Half of the week, you initiate, plan and execute hands-on research activities. The other half is used to observe and analyse user behaviour and communicate those insights effectively to various teams and stakeholders. You experiment with research approaches to answer important questions. How can we make in-app customer service more accessible?&amp;nbsp; How do customers decide what to eat?&amp;nbsp; How can we make delivering our groceries safer for our runners? Every week presents new challenges to explore, frame and evaluate. Understanding both the big picture and the details, you examine insights from unique angles to bring a deeper understanding of customer experience and provide testable hypotheses.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research:&lt;/strong&gt; Take ownership of research activities to bring deep level insights&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing &amp;amp; exploring:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide new hypotheses to test and explore&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with designers and test prototypes on a weekly basis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Share insights:&lt;/strong&gt; Document sessions and present actionable insights to both consumer-facing and employee-facing teams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer focus:&lt;/strong&gt; Be the face of Picnic and engage with customers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; Strive for continuous improvement to take our UX team to the next level&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your superpowers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;MSc. degree in a relevant field, such as Industrial Design, Human Computer Interaction Design or Product Design&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;0-3 years of experience as UX Researcher &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Strong portfolio showcasing end-to-end product thinking, solving real problems for real people at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Analytical eye: You’re not a data wizard, but you’re familiar with Excel and know how to visualise and interpret data&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ability to reason on high level about various topics, to quickly understand and discuss both business and technical concepts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Excellent communicator: You know how to strike up a conversation with anyone and know how to present insights succinctly&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Flexibility: Agile approach and ability to learn on the go&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Creativity: Outside-the box thinking and passion for details&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Affinity for or previous experience with digital design is a plus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Fluency in both Dutch and English&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Open and available to work on-site fulltime&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Picnic perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🥗Fresh Lunch, coffee, and snacks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;Our offices are equipped with fully-fledged coffee bars and a kitchen and chefs. They prepare delicious fresh and warm lunches every day so you can keep your energy up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🚴🏼‍♂️Health insurance discount &amp;amp; bike plan&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;We have a partnership with CZ (a health insurance provider). Picnic employees get a discount on CZ insurance packages between 5% and 15%. Furthermore, through our partnership with Lease a Bike, you can rent-to-own a new (e)bike at a discounted rate&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;✍🏼 Learning &amp;amp; development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;You’ll get ample opportunity to work on yourself at Picnic. We offer personal development through Lepaya courses, Academy trainings, and more. Interested in improving your mental wellbeing? Through OpenUp you get free access to trained psychologists and many courses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;All the rest&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;perks-content&quot;&gt;At Picnic you get 25 holidays, we cover your travel expenses and offer a pension plan. And your phone and laptop are on us, as well.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-intro-section&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section-inner&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;entry-intro&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In a nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Picnic operates more than 40 product tech teams that each provide an integral part of our customers&#39; experience - from the point they start the app until the moment they hold their groceries in their hands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Tech Lead you will be leading one of these teams and empower them to deliver high-quality, secure and performant solutions for the business we&#39;re building. Together with the Product Owner you will evaluate initiatives and drive roadmap discussions. You&#39;ll design and estimate technical solutions for the presented challenges together with your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for the delivery of projects and for developing the skills and strengths of the people working in your team. As a Tech Lead, you&#39;ll lead by example, not by title.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t hide what we do. Instead, we open-source with the community that helped us grow. Here&#39;s proof: &lt;a href=&quot;http://picnic.tech&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;http://picnic.tech&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shaping: &lt;/strong&gt;As a Tech Lead in one of our domains, you&#39;ll work with stakeholders from tech and business to translate requirements into scalable and resilient solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; You help the team plan, prioritize and make the right trade-offs. Ensuring business goals are achieved while also realizing your long-term technical vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;re the go-to for your product domain – both for your own team and for others who want to build on what you own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;You are able to communicate your views both when specifying new features with stakeholders and while providing technical mentorship to your colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentorship: &lt;/strong&gt;You invest in your people. Through real conversations, honest feedback, and hands-on coaching, you help them grow faster than they would anywhere else.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership: &lt;/strong&gt;You build it - you run it - you love it. You own the health of your product and the support model behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our tech&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tech:&lt;/strong&gt; Java 21/25 (Spring 6 with Spring Boot 3.5, Reactor, Immutables), Maven, RabbitMQ, Kafka, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Git, Docker, AWS, Helm, Terraform, Kubernetes, Vault, Datadog, Python 3.x, Typescript&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s Degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Information Technology, Computer Engineering or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have at least 7 years of experience and a profound understanding of back-end development including Java, Spring Boot, MongoDB and PostgreSQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have at least 2 years of experience in leading projects and/or teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have solid problem-solving skills and enjoy complex challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re based in or happy to relocate to the Netherlands. We work from our office in Amsterdam – for a Tech Lead, being present makes a genuine difference to your team and the work. There&#39;s flexibility to work from home when needed, but if remote or hybrid-first is what you&#39;re after, this probably isn&#39;t the right fit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have great English skills (no Dutch required).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Picnic Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;✍🏼 Grow faster than anywhere else&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Picnic&#39;s Tech Academy, O&#39;Reilly, leadership trainings, and Lunch &amp;amp; Learn sessions. But honestly, the fastest growth comes from the complex challenges - and we have plenty of those.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💡 Own something that matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll shape technical direction and drive outcomes that reach millions of customers across three countries. We build everything in-house, so the decisions are yours and the impact is real.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🫱🏼‍🫲🏾 A place worth showing up to&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Freshly prepared lunches, a Picnic barista, 80+ nationalities, and a social calendar from team events to our annual company ski trip.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are plenty of sports communities and events to get involved with, from tennis to yoga, to climbing!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🔋 Attractive package&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer competitive compensation and a pension plan that looks out for your future self, as well as 25 vacation days per year, so you can recharge your batteries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌍 Benefits for expats &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Relocation support, free Dutch classes, and expat integration to help you land well from day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h1&gt;In a nutshell&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the intelligence that helps households get the week sorted&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agentic grocery assistance:&lt;/strong&gt; Picnic brings together something unusually powerful for an AI builder: a direct customer relationship, a live grocery assortment and the operational system that takes every order from intention to delivery. That gives you the opportunity to build an assistant that does more than talk; it can understand a household’s plans and constraints, assemble a grounded basket, explain its choices and learn from what customers accept or change. You will decide where models, retrieval, ranking and deterministic services add real value, balancing customer control, correctness, latency, reliability and cost.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical leadership &amp;amp; vision: &lt;/strong&gt;As a Staff AI Engineer, you will be the hands-on technical lead for Agentic Shopping. You will own technical direction, architecture and model-strategy decisions; solve the hardest production challenges yourself; and establish evaluation, observability, safety and fallback patterns that other teams can reuse.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Picnic’s shopping assistant:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the technical direction for agentic shopping experiences that help millions of people plan and shop effortlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical leadership &amp;amp; architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the system architecture for multi-turn conversational agents, balancing latency, safety guardrails, and inference costs. Technically mentor engineers across the organization to execute on building production-grade agentic systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rapid prototyping &amp;amp; productionization:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive a fast-paced, iterative engineering cadence. Build initial prototypes, establish architectural patterns, and write production code when necessary to unblock complex technical challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Model fine-tuning &amp;amp; context engineering:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and implement systems architectures for multi-turn, conversational agents using open-weight models and techniques like fine-tuning, distillation, and RAG.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evaluation &amp;amp; safety feedback loops:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish continuous offline and online evaluation for mission completion, basket correctness, customer effort, clarification quality, acceptance and corrections, safety, reliability, latency and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with product, design, and product teams to define technical trade-offs, align on agent capabilities, and ensure a seamless, safe user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;We’re looking for&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of taking complex multi-turn conversational AI systems from architectural design to high-scale production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience training, fine-tuning, and optimizing open-weight LLMs for production deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on expertise building production RAG systems, context management, and state handling for multi-turn dialogues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing robust evaluation loops, continuous monitoring systems, and automated safety/guardrail mechanisms for customer-facing applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead technical direction, perform design reviews, and mentor engineering teams without relying on hierarchy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python skills and demonstrated ability to choose and productionize appropriate model, orchestration, retrieval, evaluation and inference tooling. Experience with tools such as PyTorch, LangGraph, vLLM, Pydantic AI, Qdrant or DeepEval is useful, or similar framework tools is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;+ Bonus points!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking retrieval, ranking or recommendation models from problem definition to measurable production impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth expertise in deep learning for sequence modelling, representation learning, or retrieval and ranking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in Computer Science, AI (or a related field), a PhD, open-source contributions, or peer-reviewed research are considered strong pluses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Picnic Perks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🫱🏼‍🫲🏾 Teamwork makes the dream work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With more than 80 nationalities across 3 countries, you’ll be part of a diverse company with plenty of cool stuff to get involved with, from board game evenings to after-work drinks to our company ski trip and more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💡 Make a difference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work in an awesome startup environment with the freedom to drive your own projects and create a visible impact. Our fully electric vehicles and sustainable business model mean you’ll also be contributing to making the world a better place!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🥗 Fresh Lunch, coffee, and snacks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our offices are equipped with fully-fledged coffee bars and a kitchen and chefs. They prepare delicious fresh and warm lunches every day so you can keep your energy up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🚲 Health insurance discount &amp;amp; bike plan&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a partnership with CZ (a health insurance provider). Picnic employees get a discount on CZ insurance packages between 5% and 15%. Furthermore, through our partnership with Lease a Bike, you can rent-to-own a new (e)bike at a discounted rate&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌎 Relocation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re moving from another country to join Picnic we make it as smooth as possible for you. We’ll cover your flight costs for you and your partner and kids, your first month&#39;s rent and moving costs (up to €2000), and help you with the 30% tax ruling setup and application.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📆 All the rest&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Picnic you get 25 holidays, we cover your travel expenses and offer a pension plan. And your phone and laptop are on us, as well.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In a nutshell&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a developer working with Salesforce and Python, you&#39;ll join the Master Data team. We own the product data everything else runs on — from integrating supplier catalogues, through enrichment and validation, to what a customer sees in the app and what the warehouse needs to plan how a product fits in a tote. Hundreds of colleagues work with the platform every day, handling large volumes of master data across multiple countries, and your job is to make that easier — a validation that catches a bad value before it reaches a customer, a screen that stops taking eight clicks to do one thing. You&#39;ll solve data issues and steadily improve the platform. Over time the role grows towards software engineering, deeper into Python and data platform architecture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Take ownership of a part of the platform, know it well, and grow into the person others come to for it. You&#39;ll propose improvements rather than waiting for them to be assigned, and you try things and iterate quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain and extend:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, test, evolve, and refine the core aspects of our master data platform with a creative and analytical approach. Keep it healthy by improving existing flows and integrations while reducing complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data modeling and quality: &lt;/strong&gt;Shape how product information is modeled, and build the validation, enrichment and monitoring that keeps it accurate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work with your users: &lt;/strong&gt;Build relationships with the operational teams who work daily with the platform, understand their pain points, and turn those into improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code Review:&lt;/strong&gt; Review designs and code of teammates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Support existing products and work with other developers to resolve incidents, including occasional on-call shifts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technologies we use&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce: Apex, LWCs, RESTful integrations, Salesforce Connect&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deployments: Salesforce DX &amp;amp; Unlocked Packages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IDEs: VSCode, Intellij; scratch orgs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python: FastAPI, Pydantic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data: SQL, Snowflake, dbt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Version Control: Git, Github&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD: TeamCity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering or a related quantitative field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience with Salesforce implementations including Apex&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and detail-oriented: you pick things up fast, including technologies new to you, like Python or dbt, and you have the patience to chase an inconsistency until you understand where it came from. Using AI tools effectively in your daily work is good evidence of both&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuinely interested in data and the people who depend on it — models, quality, what happens downstream&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid judgement on tradeoffs between configuration and custom code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applies software engineering best practices to Apex/LWC development e.g. triggers, async apex, testing, access and data lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;English skills are on point (no Dutch required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bonus Points!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good command of Python/Java&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with master data, product data management or data engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of DX and unlocked packages&lt;/li&gt;
